From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:27:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] media: iris: return no picture for a frame the gen1
 firmware drops

For a frame that is decoded but not shown, such as a VP9 alt-ref frame
packed in a superframe, the gen1 firmware returns the OUTPUT2 buffer with
HFI_BUFFERFLAG_DROP_FRAME and the filled length of a whole picture
(3133440 bytes at 1080p). iris flagged the buffer V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR
but kept that length and the timestamp. Chromium's stateful decoder
outputs every CAPTURE buffer whose bytesused is not zero and does not
look at the error flag.

venus returns such a buffer with no payload and no timestamp, and
msm_vidc with no payload. Do the same. Valve's startup_machine.webm, a
clip the Steam client plays, has 11 hidden frames in 94 packets.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
index bfd7495bf44f..b28617469123 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
@@ -519,8 +519,12 @@ static void iris_hfi_gen1_session_ftb_done(struct iris_inst *inst, void *packet)
 	if (hfi_flags & HFI_BUFFERFLAG_DATACORRUPT)
 		flags |= V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
 
-	if (hfi_flags & HFI_BUFFERFLAG_DROP_FRAME)
+	/* A frame not to be shown (VP9 hidden frame): no picture, as on venus */
+	if (hfi_flags & HFI_BUFFERFLAG_DROP_FRAME) {
 		flags |= V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
+		buf->data_size = 0;
+		buf->timestamp = 0;
+	}
 
 	buf->flags |= flags;
 
